From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32: name dialog controls' resources as ReactOS does for its shell

Purpose: show the images of ReactOS's shell dialogs (msgina's Shut Down
and Log Off dialogs: the banner and the icons).
ReactOS behavior: ReactOS's user32 creates a dialog control whose title
is a resource number with the title "#number"
(win32ss/user/user32/windows/dialog.c), and ReactOS's Common Controls 6
static control loads its bitmap or icon from that name as it is.
Wine before: like Windows, Wine passes the number as 0xffff followed by
the number. ReactOS's static control, which ReactOS's explorer uses
through its manifest, passed that to LoadImage, which found nothing, so
the dialogs showed no banner and no icons.
Change: with WIN4WINE_SHELL=reactos, title such controls "#number".
Evidence: +resource traces; the dialogs' screenshots.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_SHELL=reactos.
---
 dlls/user32/dialog.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/user32/dialog.c b/dlls/user32/dialog.c
index 4e4a682..478bd00 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/dialog.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/dialog.c
@@ -214,13 +214,20 @@ static BOOL DIALOG_CreateControls32( HWND hwnd, LPCSTR template, const DLG_TEMPL
         if (unicode)
         {
             const WCHAR *caption = info.windowName;
-            WCHAR caption_buf[3];
+            WCHAR caption_buf[8];
 
             if (IS_INTRESOURCE(caption) && caption)
             {
-                caption_buf[0] = 0xffff;
-                caption_buf[1] = PtrToUlong( caption );
-                caption_buf[2] = 0;
+                /* ReactOS's user32 names a control's resource "#id", and ReactOS's
+                 * controls (its shell's Common Controls 6) only read that form. */
+                if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_REACTOS)
+                    swprintf( caption_buf, ARRAY_SIZE(caption_buf), L"#%u", PtrToUlong( caption ) );
+                else
+                {
+                    caption_buf[0] = 0xffff;
+                    caption_buf[1] = PtrToUlong( caption );
+                    caption_buf[2] = 0;
+                }
                 caption = caption_buf;
             }
 
